      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Cannabinoid CB(1) receptor agonists exhibit potent analgesic effects in rodents and humans, but their clinical utility as analgesic drugs is often limited by centrally mediated side effects. We report herein the preparation of N-methyl-3-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-2,3,4,9-tetrahydro-1H-carbazole-6-carboxamides as a novel class of hCB(1)/hCB(2) dual agonists with attractive physicochemical properties. More specifically, (R)-N,9-dimethyl-N-(4-(methylamino)-4-oxobutyl)-3-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-2,3,4,9-tetrahydro-1H-carbazole-6-carboxamide, displayed an extremely low level of CNS penetration (Rat Cbr/Cplasma=0.005 or 0.5%) and was devoid of CNS side effects during pharmaco-dynamic testing."
      },
